for which the compile might be able to determine at compile time that you're not writing a tag whose length won't fit in 16 bits.

(This requires !10048 to be merged, so that the fact that `wtap_buffer_append_epdu_tag()` does *not* modify the tag data passed to it is indicated in its declaration.)

